// Written by `claude-sync setup`, which replaces any local edits on each run.
// Everything in ~/.claude syncs except what is meaningless or harmful on another machine.
// (?d) lets Syncthing delete this machine's ignored files along with their directory, when
// another device deletes it or a joining device discards its own. Without it the directory
// stays, and a join never finishes.

// Login token: one per device.
/.credentials.json

// Named after a process ID on one machine.
(?d)/sessions/*.json
(?d)/sessions/*.key

// Held by a process on one machine.
/.update.lock
(?d)/ide/*.lock
(?d)/tasks/*/.lock
(?d)/plugins/cache/**/.in_use

// Git clones each machine pulls on its own; syncing one .git between two pullers corrupts it.
(?d)/plugins/marketplaces

// This machine's daemon, session environments, shell snapshots and unsent telemetry.
/daemon
/session-env
/shell-snapshots
/telemetry

// Half-written files mid-save: Claude Code names them <file>.tmp.<8 hex> or
// <file>.tmp.<pid>.<12 hex>. Hex digits are listed out because Syncthing's glob takes only
// one range per [] class, and rejects the whole file on [0-9a-f].
(?d)*.tmp.[0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef]
(?d)*.tmp.[0-9]*.[0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef][0123456789abcdef]
